=== Time-measurement ===
The rendering-time is an approximate estimate of time. If a file renders correctly, the maximal time should be limited to 1-Minutes, if a file is not rendered correctly a penalty of 10 times of the slowest renderer (max. 10Minutes) but at least 1Minute should be counted. For unclear (e.g. unprecise) renderings the rendertime should be set to the slowest (correct) renderer. Runs should be limited to one CPU.

This indices should be used for the times
# However current times by [[User:JoKalliauer]] do not account for those penalties, therefore renderer which do not support features pretend to be fast, because they don't support computationally intensive features. The tests were done on a 4-CPU-Notebook with AMD A12-9700P RADEON R7; 1.3GHz-2.5GHz on Ferdora 33 (Linux). The processes were not limited to one CPU. The time is the difference between the modified time of the first and the last file, so the rendering of the first PNG is not included.
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RazrFalcon/resvg-test-suite/master/official.csv (from Jun 2020)
-->

