== Renderers ==

Tested:
* [[:w:librsvg]], a small, simple viewer to preview how SVG files will look when rendered by MediaWiki
* [https://github.com/RazrFalcon/resvg/ resvg], one of the fastest and most correct SVG renderers<ref>[[User:JoKalliauer/SVG_test_suites]]</ref>, implemented in Rust
* [[:w:Inkscape|Inkscape]], which also supports some Inkscape-specific (non-standard) SVG features
* [https://xmlgraphics.apache.org/batik/ Apache Batik], an SVG toolkit implemented in Java

Others (not tested here):
* [https://github.com/tibold/svg-explorer-extension svg-explorer-extension], a free software extension for {{w|Windows Explorer}} that generates thumbnails for SVG files
* [https://github.com/shakiba/svgexport svgexport], a Node.js rasterizing module
* [https://cairosvg.org/ CairoSVG], a Python converter using Cairo
* [[w:ImageMagick|ImageMagick]], a leading free software imaging software suite
* [https://github.com/svg-net/SVG SVG.NET], a cross-platform C# library which can render SVG
* [https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtsvg-index.html Qt SVG], a C++ module for Qt
* [http://wxsvg.sourceforge.net/ wxSVG], a C++ library to create, manipulate and render SVG files with the [[w:wxWidgets|wxWidgets]] toolkit
* [https://pypi.org/project/svglib/ svglib], a Python library
* [https://products.aspose.com/svg/net Aspose.SVG], a commercial SVG library for .NET
